{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1274358-breaking-points-and-supernaturals","id":1274358,"title":"Breaking points and supernaturals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-14T06:52:54-08:00","id":1274358,"title":"Breaking points and supernaturals","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I have doubts on breaking points and creatures with a different Integrity-like stat, do Integrity breaking points apply to them too? If so, do merits like Support Network, affect them too? My current understanding would be:<br /> <br /> Clarity: Not affected, but can use Support Network<br /> Cover: Not affected, no Support Network<br /> Harmony: Not affected, no Support Network<br /> Humanity: Affected, and can use Support Network<br /> Pilgrimage: Not affected, but can use Support Network<br /> Wisdom: Not affected, but can use Support Network<br /> <br /> However, I would like to know if this is covered somewhere and I am just speculating.<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 12-15-2018, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T07:16:40-08:00","id":1274361,"title":"","content":"Integrity breaking points only apply to Integrity, but some Integrity equivalents does have overlap in what can be a breaking point. They do so for different reasons, though.<br /> A human committing murder face a breaking point because it's a traumatic experience. A vampire committing murder face a breaking point because it's an act that resonates much closer to their beastly instincts and pushes away the humanity that they otherwise cling to (unless they're already monstrous enough that it won't push them further away from their human nature). A mage committing murder face a breaking point because murder is a drastic measure that shows that you don't have control (and in opposition to the former two, the more the murder is deliberated and planned, the lesser the breaking point is).<br /> <br /> I do think that Humanity is the trait that could work most with Support Network (but limited to Touchstone interactions and has a lower dot rating maximum, if I were to rewrite it) followed by Wisdom, but by the book Support Network (and other Merits that specify they work with Integrity) does not apply to any other Integrity equivalent trait. Expanding it and other similar effects to other traits would be a house rule and thus something that has to be discussed and approved at each individual table.<br /> <br /> Side note: Clarity could work, but only if the support network consists of other changelings and/or fae-touched since deprogramming and similar psychological techniques are <i>harmful</i> to Clarity in second edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T08:46:18-08:00","id":1274567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1274358-breaking-points-and-supernaturals?p=1274361#post1274361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Integrity breaking points only apply to Integrity, but some Integrity equivalents does have overlap in what can be a breaking point. They do so for different reasons, though.<br /> A human committing murder face a breaking point because it's a traumatic experience. A vampire committing murder face a breaking point because it's an act that resonates much closer to their beastly instincts and pushes away the humanity that they otherwise cling to (unless they're already monstrous enough that it won't push them further away from their human nature). A mage committing murder face a breaking point because murder is a drastic measure that shows that you don't have control (and in opposition to the former two, the more the murder is deliberated and planned, the lesser the breaking point is).<br /> <br /> I do think that Humanity is the trait that could work most with Support Network (but limited to Touchstone interactions and has a lower dot rating maximum, if I were to rewrite it) followed by Wisdom, but by the book Support Network (and other Merits that specify they work with Integrity) does not apply to any other Integrity equivalent trait. Expanding it and other similar effects to other traits would be a house rule and thus something that has to be discussed and approved at each individual table.<br /> <br /> Side note: Clarity could work, but only if the support network consists of other changelings and/or fae-touched since deprogramming and similar psychological techniques are <i>harmful</i> to Clarity in second edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer, I go by the rules as written, but I thought that at least Clarity, Humanity, Pilgrimage and Wisdom would have been touched by Support Network.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}